280351778243a0386934d839b8849a03d68b4eebfe437030fa7414e5eaba","file":"preprints/The-Approximation-Threshold-for-Metric-k-Median-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":25,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"654a5eb2e117adac4bc6ed0a464e05ad8b1aa42ac6bd6d4fecb1acb0095320d1","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Approximation-Threshold-for-Metric-k-Median-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:b8d7280351778243a0386934d839b8849a03d68b4eebfe437030fa7414e5eaba","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Approximation-Threshold-for-Metric-k-Median-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L25"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every fixed \\(\\varepsilon>0\\), there is a deterministic algorithm which,\ngiven a finite rational metric \\(k\\)-median instance with \\(1\\le k\\le |F|\\),\nreturns \\(S\\subseteq F\\), \\(|S|\\le k\\), such that\n\\[\n \\sum_{j\\in J}d(j,S)\\le\n \\left(1+\\frac2e+\\varepsilon\\right)\\OPT_k.\n\\]\nIts running time is polynomial in the binary encoding length of the instance.\nThe polynomial may depend on \\(\\varepsilon\\)."}
